                <pb facs="0823" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.4116/108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-18T20:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                                1920—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 18—7:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1633. It was decided by the Cabinet this morning to proceed with the project for
                    trade with Soviet Russia. For that purpose the Cabinet gave its approval to the
                    resumption of trade negotiations with Krassin immediately.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
